  "aciklama": "Ajka flooded villages with caustic red mud. The cause: structural failure of a reservoir dyke holding highly alkaline bauxite residue.\n\nFailure chain: Red mud stored behind dyke → Wall weakens → Corner breaches → Caustic mud floods villages → Rivers contaminated\n\nRelated episode: Deepwater Horizon: The Test Result Nobody Believed — https://youtu.be/aScjSrwqeRk\n\nFootage & sources:\n• Archival film: \"Devecser, 10.10.2010 - panoramio.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Devecser%2C_10.10.2010_-_panoramio.jpg\n• Archival film: \"Marcal 2010 10 12.JPG\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Marcal_2010_10_12.JPG\n• Archival film: \"Toxic Sludge in Hungary 2010.jpg\" — Wikimedia Commons (public domain / free licence): https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Toxic_Sludge_in_Hungary_2010.jpg\n\nTechnical references:\n• Wikipedia — Ajka alumina plant accident — https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ajka_alumina_plant_accident\n• Government source — 20966220 (cited by Wikipedia) — https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/20966220\n\nNarration uses a synthetic voice. Footage is real archival film or licensed stock; anything reconstructed is labelled on screen.\n\nFailure File · Episode 29 · A new engineering failure, reconstructed every day.\n\n#shorts #engineering #Ajka #industrial #history",
